{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/290752.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS KENT-637A44: Kent-637A44. Roman. Coin. AS or Dupondius of Antoninus Pius. Reverse view."]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["moneta"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (moneta)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["138-161 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Kent (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Iscrizione o legenda"]},"value":{"none":["SA(LVS AVG)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["Possible 138-161AD. Antoninus Pius As or Dupondius. Length 25.7mm, Width 25mm, Thickness 3mm, Diameter 25.7mm, Weight 9g. Obverse: Laureate or bare bust right. Inscription: Illegible. Reverse: Standing figure probably Salus at an altar, feeding a snake with 'S(C)' in the field. Inscription: SA(LVS AVG). Mint name: Rome. Die axis: 300 deg. or 10 o'clock. Worn and very corroded especially the obverse. However, there are some traces of intact green patina on the reverse and a few of the letters are legible. Ref. Coins of England and the UK, Spink 2009, page 52"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["KENT-637A44"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["290752"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: , Geoff Burr, 2010-03-09 13:13:44, CC BY-SA 4.0 ; None, Geoff Burr, 2010-03-09 13:13:44, CC BY-SA 2.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/290752","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS KENT-637A44: Kent-637A44. Roman. Coin. AS or Dupondius of Antoninus Pius. Reverse view.